# L §5.7 Reads and lifespans: "a governing row is read even outside a lifespan; with none, a read outside the
# lifespan is none, inside it HOLE-UNGOVERNED" (L §4.6 step 5).  ana lives 2000-01-01..2020-12-31; x has a row
# for ana only from 2023 (after her life): read in 2025 it is the row, in 2021 none, in 2010 a hole.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

kind persons

input x[p in persons]: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2023..
  known 2025-01-01
  persons + [ana] lives 2000-01-01..2020-12-31
  x[ana] = 5

ask q1: x[ana] law 2025-01-01
ask q2: x[ana] law 2021-01-01
ask q3: x[ana] law 2010-01-01
=== expect
q1: 5
  law date 2025-01-01, cut 2026-01-01
q2: none
  law date 2021-01-01, cut 2026-01-01
q3: ?"x at ana: no value at 2010-01-01" (x[ana])
  law date 2010-01-01, cut 2026-01-01
